{"event_type":"review","id":"cc0893c04cfe14fcd4872fc57788475d5a1d33d61fdaee3879952413e52917ff","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T19:59:30Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6615554f8c017891713cb100cbbb03ff72fa9375e6a038b0a04d0e4b51aa3db7","sha256":"6615554f8c017891713cb100cbbb03ff72fa9375e6a038b0a04d0e4b51aa3db7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cfda3886a69a88dfdc593a039282a59ed1ab9e16f64612807bb883b3ddb88f17","sha256":"cfda3886a69a88dfdc593a039282a59ed1ab9e16f64612807bb883b3ddb88f17"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/54f899a1a758ccb699a8108e82176ac619edb045eb3ab08a63530a2c678e2e00","sha256":"54f899a1a758ccb699a8108e82176ac619edb045eb3ab08a63530a2c678e2e00"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d65edd1ddb40bb8638f951afc0b21fc702744263fc26221b63725a69db2a9755","sha256":"d65edd1ddb40bb8638f951afc0b21fc702744263fc26221b63725a69db2a9755"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1665f7403aa92e1e492316066cf3875b0d5b18cc535c6a254cf11b498c768c6d","sha256":"1665f7403aa92e1e492316066cf3875b0d5b18cc535c6a254cf11b498c768c6d"}],"attempt_id":"c2cbc2a5625bc758c37cc4481790704cd98129280bffa2d35d9b5942aee16ca2:0:1","base":"cb2dccfc2d190481901924a07875b223a4c70a9f","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"61d531d20afff9e290692498422c6fb2f9427e31","body":"**Forward SIGHUP from the build wrapper to its active child.**\n\nNode ends a process on SIGHUP by default. `scripts/build.mjs` registers listeners only for SIGINT and SIGTERM, so a SIGHUP sent to the build PID ends the wrapper. The current child is spawned without `detached` and receives no signal, so it can keep running and write `dist` after the build exits. The build is not marked complete on this path. The gap is in `build.mjs` itself, so it applies both when `enterResourceScope` takes its unscoped fallback and inside the scoped child, which uses the same two-signal list.\n\nAdd SIGHUP to the forwarded signals, as the resource-scope helper already does. With the listener in place, the active child receives SIGHUP and exits. Its null status resolves to 1, so the wrapper exits with status 1 before `markBuildComplete()` runs.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    for (const signal of ['SIGINT', 'SIGTERM']) process.once(signal, () => child.kill(signal));\n+    for (const signal of ['SIGINT', 'SIGTERM', 'SIGHUP']) process.once(signal, () => child.kill(signal));\n```\n\n</details>","id":"a522487ad4df35d22d8d813d8237df28a3e0c8cc73e855b77caab8b90e1a13d2","intervals":[[16,16]],"path":"scripts/build.mjs","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Forward SIGHUP from the build wrapper to its active child."}],"head":"fe90e2fddc6be0820bf32545a2f70e45e8dca2ec","head_tree":"12e1095fbecea104e28eb07c86b1760f1f72bd77","input_scope":[{"blob":"61d531d20afff9e290692498422c6fb2f9427e31","intervals":[[1,27]],"path":"scripts/build.mjs"},{"blob":"0a6409e3c3f6d020810cbaab9e3c0672703e00bb","intervals":[[1,18]],"path":"scripts/emit-queue-runner-capabilities.mjs"}],"job_id":"c2cbc2a5625bc758c37cc4481790704cd98129280bffa2d35d9b5942aee16ca2:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"61d531d20afff9e290692498422c6fb2f9427e31","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"scripts/build.mjs","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"0a6409e3c3f6d020810cbaab9e3c0672703e00bb","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"scripts/emit-queue-runner-capabilities.mjs","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"61d531